### ENGINEERING EXECUTION RULES

Use this workflow:

PHASE 1 — Repository Discovery and Audit.

PHASE 2 — Architecture and Gap Assessment.

PHASE 3 — Cryptographic Module Boundary Design.

PHASE 4 — Security Architecture Implementation.

PHASE 5 — Approved-Mode Implementation.

PHASE 6 — Self-Test and Failure Handling.

PHASE 7 — Platform Integration.

PHASE 8 — Automated Testing and Independent Code Review.

PHASE 9 — Documentation and Evidence Generation.

PHASE 10 — External Laboratory Readiness Assessment.

Do not skip phases.

Before implementing major changes, provide a proposed change plan and identify potential breaking changes.

Run actual tests after implementation.

For every finding, classify it as:

- PASS — Evidence supports the requirement.
- FAIL — A verified requirement violation exists.
- PARTIAL — Some implementation exists but evidence is incomplete.
- NOT IMPLEMENTED — Required functionality is missing.
- NOT APPLICABLE — Supported by documented technical reasoning.
- EXTERNAL VALIDATION REQUIRED — Requires independent laboratory assessment.

A successful local test must never be represented as a completed CMVP validation.

